              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Standards of Ethics of The American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) apply to all currently or formerly certified/registered individuals, and to applicants. Radiologic Technology encompasses disciplines like radiography, radiation therapy, nuclear medicine, and more."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Statement of Purpose:",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " The primary purpose of these ethics requirements is to identify individuals who have internalized professional values that lead them to act in the best interests of patients. These standards provide proactive guidance, promote ethical behavior, and support ARRT's mission of high standards in patient care by restricting those who exhibit inconsistent behavior."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Standards consist of two main parts: the Code of Ethics and the Rules of Ethics."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
