      {
        "title": "Introduction to ARRT Standards of Ethics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Standards of Ethics of The American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) apply to all currently or formerly certified/registered individuals, and to applicants. Radiologic Technology encompasses disciplines like radiography, radiation therapy, nuclear medicine, and more."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Statement of Purpose:",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " The primary purpose of these ethics requirements is to identify individuals who have internalized professional values that lead them to act in the best interests of patients. These standards provide proactive guidance, promote ethical behavior, and support ARRT's mission of high standards in patient care by restricting those who exhibit inconsistent behavior."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Standards consist of two main parts: the Code of Ethics and the Rules of Ethics."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The ARRT Code of Ethics - Guiding Principles (Part 1)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Code of Ethics"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is an aspirational guide for professional conduct related to patients, employers, colleagues, and other healthcare team members."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Key Principles Include:",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 1:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Act professionally, respond to patient needs, and support colleagues."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 2:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Advance the profession's objective to serve humanity with dignity."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 3:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Deliver care unrestricted by personal attributes or illness, without discrimination."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 4:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Practice based on theory, use equipment appropriately, employ proper procedures."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 5:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Assess situations, exercise care and judgment, assume responsibility, act in patient's best interest."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A technologist refuses to provide care to a patient based on their national origin. This directly violates which principle of the Code of Ethics?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Principle 1",
              "Principle 3",
              "Principle 5"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Principle 3 states: \"The Registered Technologist delivers patient care and service... without discrimination on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, national origin...\"."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The ARRT Code of Ethics - Guiding Principles (Part 2)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Continuing with the aspirational Code of Ethics:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 6:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Act as an agent by observation and communication for diagnosis/treatment."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 7:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Use equipment and procedures to minimize radiation exposure."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 8:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Practice ethically and protect patient's right to quality care."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 9:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Respect patient confidences and privacy."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 10:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Continually strive to improve knowledge and skills."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Principle 11:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Refrain from using illegal drugs or substances impairing judgment."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An RTT discussing a patient's identifiable medical information with a friend outside of work, without any legal requirement or welfare concern, would violate Principle 9 of the Code of Ethics."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Yes",
              "No"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Yes, Principle 9 emphasizes respecting patient confidences and privacy."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Introduction to the ARRT Rules of Ethics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Rules of Ethics"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " are "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "mandatory and enforceable"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " standards of minimally acceptable professional conduct."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Key Points:",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Enforceable:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Violations are subject to sanctions."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Duty to Report:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " RTTs must notify ARRT of ethics violations (own or others') within 30 days or at annual renewal. Applicants must report within 30 days of occurrence."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page4_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Are the ARRT Rules of Ethics merely suggestions for best practice?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Yes",
              "No"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "No, the Rules of Ethics are mandatory and enforceable."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Highlights from the Rules of Ethics - Part 1",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Violations subject RTTs/Candidates to sanctions. Categories include:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "1. Fraud or Deceptive Practices: In procuring/maintaining certification, employment, or licenses. False/misleading communications about credentials. Fraudulent billing."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "2. Subversion: Subverting ARRT exams, CQR, or Education Requirements. Failure to cooperate with ARRT investigations."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sharing specific questions remembered from an ARRT certification exam with students preparing for the exam is acceptable professional behavior."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Yes",
              "No"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "No, this is a form of examination subversion."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Highlights from the Rules of Ethics - Part 2",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "3. Unprofessional Conduct: Incl. failure to conform to standards, sexual misconduct, conduct likely to deceive/harm."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "4. Scope of Practice Violations: Performing procedures not competent to do, improper delegation."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "5. Fitness to Practice: Inability to practice safely due to illness, alcohol/drugs, mental/physical condition."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "6. Improper Management of Patient Records: False entries, failing to protect confidential info."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An RTT documents that a complex procedure was performed when, in fact, a simpler version was done. Is this an ethical violation?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Yes",
              "No"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Yes, this would be improper management of patient records and potentially fraudulent."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Highlights from the Rules of Ethics - Part 3 & Duty to Report",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "7. Violation of State/Federal Law or Regulatory Rule: Incl. narcotics laws, licensure actions, criminal proceedings."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "8. Duty to Report: Knowing of a violation by any RTT/Candidate and failing to promptly report to ARRT. Failing to immediately report to one's supervisor an error made in patient care that could be harmful, unethical, or improper."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You have reviewed the core components of the ARRT Standards of Ethics."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Click \"Start Activity\" below to proceed to the Case Study Activity."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
